{
  "format": "Device-data exporters (storage.ts export*AsJson / export*AsCsv). kind=<rows>_<json|csv>, rows being entries (LogEntry[]), ranked_dishes, ranked_foods, favorites or custom_foods: input is the row array -> the exported string, byte for byte. JSON is 2-space-indented JSON.stringify of the rows (integral numbers print without a decimal point). CSV is a header line then one line per row joined by LF with no trailing newline; every field is double-quoted with embedded quotes doubled, and a field whose text starts with = + - or @ gets a tab inserted after the opening quote. Input key order is the output key order. Every case is {kind, name, input, expected}; expected is what shared/src (TypeScript) returns for input. JSON null = a value that is present and null. An ABSENT key = undefined / not set: implementations must treat a missing key and an unset field as the same thing, and must not emit null for it. Regenerate with `pnpm --filter @udine/shared vectors`; never hand-edit expected.",
